# The agent may propose changes to any of this. It may not merge them.
#
# `main` requires code-owner review, so a pull request touching these paths cannot merge until
# lldata approves it — whatever the agent concludes about its own authority, and whatever
# AGENTS.md is edited to say in the same pull request. That last point is why this file exists
# rather than a paragraph: a rule written only in prose is one the agent can rewrite in the
# change that breaks it.
#
# What is protected is anything that constrains or observes the agent:
#
#   - the workflows, which GitHub already refuses to let a GitHub App touch
#   - the scripts, which include the checks that make a silent or failed run visible
#   - AGENTS.md, which is the authorisation rules themselves
#   - the skills, which are the procedures it follows
#   - the release path: the publishing configuration in the root build, and the single
#     `version=` line that decides what the two artifacts are called
#
# Its craft is not protected. The generator, the annotations, the example and the changelog are
# ordinary work, and a green build is a better judge of those than a human skim.

/.github/                @lldata
/.claude/                @lldata
/AGENTS.md               @lldata
/CLAUDE.md               @lldata
/build.gradle.kts        @lldata
/gradle.properties       @lldata
